# JustDubit — Full LTX-2 Pipeline on Windows (Fresh Start)

We are abandoning the Wav2Lip "Ultra-Lite" dead-end and running the **real** JustDubit pipeline:
[JustDubitPipeline](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-pipelines/src/ltx_pipelines/pipeline_justdubit.py#95-497) → LTX-2 19B model → proper audio-visual diffusion dubbing.

The codebase was written for Linux. We adapt it for Windows, download ~40 GB of weights, and wire the existing React UI to the real backend.

---

## ⚠️ User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **~40 GB download required.** The following files will be downloaded from HuggingFace into `c:\just-dub-it\weights\`:
>
> | File | Size | Source |
> |------|------|--------|
> | `ltx-2-19b-dev.safetensors` | ~35 GB | `Lightricks/LTX-2` |
> | `ltx-2-19b-distilled-lora-384.safetensors` | ~700 MB | `Lightricks/LTX-2` |
> | `ltx-2-spatial-upscaler-x2-1.0.safetensors` | ~360 MB | `Lightricks/LTX-2` |
> | `ltx-2-19b-ic-lora-lipdubbing.safetensors` | ~700 MB | `justdubit/justdubit` |
> | Gemma `gemma-3-12b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized` | ~7 GB | `google/` HuggingFace |
>
> Total: **~44 GB**. Downloads run in background via `huggingface-hub`. The UI and server stay operational during download.

> [!WARNING]
> **GTX 1050 Ti VRAM Limit (4 GB).** The full 35 GB model cannot fit in VRAM.
> We will run in **CPU offload mode** (`device_map="sequential"` / tiling enabled). This is slower but produces correct output — much better than the Wav2Lip placeholder.

